# GLO: volume, DJ filter, reso, FX 1 and FX 2 (type, amount, parameter), the four knobs, the master compressor; the list scrolls
tap GLO
expect view 3
# VOLUME is the MASTER knob while that is the volume: the row says so and does not change
turn K1 1
turn K2 1
expectvol 90
# DJ filter and resonance are rows of their own (the middle is off)
turn K1 1
expectdj 0 64
turn K2 -5
expectdj 0 54
turn K1 1
turn K2 4
expectdj 1 48
# FX2 TYPE: starts as the reverb; stepping on skips the delay (FX 1 is the delay: one buffer each), wraps at both ends
turn K1 1
expectfxtype 0 1
turn K1 1
turn K1 1
turn K1 1
expectfxtype 1 0
turn K2 1
expectfxtype 1 2
turn K2 -1
expectfxtype 1 0
turn K2 -1
expectfxtype 1 13
turn K2 1
expectfxtype 1 0
# FX2 AMOUNT and PARAM are numbers
turn K1 1
turn K2 1
expectfxamt 1 102
turn K1 1
turn K2 1
expectfxpar 1 66
shot glo_fx2.png
# FX1: PARAM, AMOUNT, then TYPE (delay -> drive)
turn K1 -1
turn K1 -1
turn K1 -1
turn K2 5
expectfxpar 0 60
turn K1 -1
turn K2 -3
expectfxamt 0 94
turn K1 -1
turn K2 1
expectfxtype 0 2
shot glo_fx1.png
# the VOLUME row counts once MASTER is given another job (the MASTER KNOB row is the eleventh)
turn K1 1
turn K1 1
turn K1 1
turn K1 1
turn K1 1
turn K1 1
turn K2 1
expectknob 0 1
turn K1 -1
turn K1 -1
turn K1 -1
turn K1 -1
turn K1 -1
turn K1 -1
turn K1 -1
turn K1 -1
turn K1 -1
turn K2 -10
expectvol 70
# the compressor rows: THRESH (95), RATIO (2), ATTACK, RELEASE, MAKEUP, MIX
turn K1 1
turn K1 1
turn K1 1
turn K1 1
turn K1 1
turn K1 1
turn K1 1
turn K1 1
turn K1 1
turn K1 1
turn K1 1
turn K1 1
turn K1 1
turn K2 -10
expectcomp 0 75
shot glo_comp.png
